            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection: is there a metabolic association?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>457-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0267659113489331</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection is an uncommon cause of chest pain and acute myocardial infarction, occurring most classically in young women without cardiovascular risk factors. We present a case of a man presenting with chest pain and arrhythmia found to have multivessel spontaneous coronary artery dissection and hyperhomocysteinemia and we raise the possibility of a potential link between the two conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
